{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1920,
 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1983, a brand-new jet ran out of fuel at 41,000 feet.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 4.49
  },
  {
   "text": "Both engines went silent, and most cockpit screens went black.",
   "s": 4.79,
   "e": 7.968
  },
  {
   "text": "A tiny emergency propeller popped out of the belly, just to keep the controls working.",
   "s": 8.268,
   "e": 12.546
  },
  {
   "text": "Sixty-nine people were now riding a giant paper airplane over Canada.",
   "s": 12.846,
   "e": 16.766
  },
  {
   "text": "So how does a jet run out of fuel?",
   "s": 17.066,
   "e": 18.535
  },
  {
   "text": "Canada was going metric, and the fuel got worked out in pounds, not kilograms.",
   "s": 18.955,
   "e": 23.1
  },
  {
   "text": "So the plane took off with less than half the fuel it needed.",
   "s": 23.4,
   "e": 25.989
  },
  {
   "text": "But the captain, Bob Pearson, happened to fly gliders for fun.",
   "s": 26.289,
   "e": 29.394
  },
  {
   "text": "His co-pilot remembered an old air force base nearby: Gimli.",
   "s": 29.694,
   "e": 33.04
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it got worse: Gimli wasn't an air base anymore.",
   "s": 33.34,
   "e": 35.786
  },
  {
   "text": "Now it was a drag strip, with a car race and campers beside the runway.",
   "s": 36.086,
   "e": 39.487
  },
  {
   "text": "The racers looked up and saw a silent airliner heading straight for them.",
   "s": 39.787,
   "e": 43.039
  },
  {
   "text": "They came in way too high. So Pearson pulled a glider trick.",
   "s": 43.339,
   "e": 46.168
  },
  {
   "text": "He flew the jet sideways to dump speed.",
   "s": 46.468,
   "e": 48.355
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the nose gear collapsed, and sparks shot down the runway.",
   "s": 48.655,
   "e": 51.385
  },
  {
   "text": "The jet skidded to a stop in front of the stunned racers.",
   "s": 51.685,
   "e": 54.203
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody was seriously hurt.",
   "s": 54.503,
   "e": 55.723
  },
  {
   "text": "The plane flew for 25 more years, with a new name: the Gimli Glider.",
   "s": 56.023,
   "e": 59.758
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow for a new weird true story every day.",
   "s": 60.058,
   "e": 62.082
  }
 ],
